DEBUGGER(2)           FORTH LEVEL DEBUGGER FUNCTIONS                DEBUGGER(2)NAME       debugger - forth level debugger; trace, break and profileSYNOPSIS       #include debugger.f83       debugger ( -- )       ADVICE ( -- ) private       +block ( advice -- block) private       +entry ( advice -- entry) private       +advice ( advice -- advice) private       +profile ( advice -- profile) private       [advice] ( advice -- ) private       [colon] ( advice -- ) private       [trace] ( advice -- ) private       [break] ( advice -- ) private       tail-recurse ( -- ) compilation immediate       ?advice ( entry -- flag)       advice ( action -- )       colon ( -- )       trace ( -- )       break ( -- )       .r ( n w -- )       .profile ( -- )       : ( -- )DESCRIPTION       Forth level debugger package. Allows basic black-box tracing of       colon definitions, break on function call and profiling of function       calls. The debugger is built on a general advice package so that       it may easily be extended with addition debugging functions. The       advice concept is a function may be asked for advice to handle a        colon definition. The trace advice function wraps the function        call in printing of the stack status and the name of the function.debugger ( -- )       Vocabulary containing the debugger definitions.ADVICE ( -- ) private       The advice structure type. Allows general handling of execution       of code definitions.+block ( advice -- block) private       Access field to code block of advice colon definition. Stored       as a pointer to threaded code.+entry ( advice -- entry) private       Access field to entry with advice block. Allows access of entry       fields such as name, link, etc. Stored as a pointer to an entry.+advice ( advice -- advice) private       Access field to advice function which is called to handle the       code block. The advice function is call with execute thus it       is a pointer to an entry. Three predefined advice functions       are available for profiling, tracing and break points.       +profile ( advice -- profile) private       Access field to counter for number of function calls. Basic       profiling information. Updated by the advice primitives.[advice] ( advice -- ) private       Management function to allow interception of function call and       calling of advice function.[colon] ( advice -- ) private       Primitive advice function call for normal function call and       increment of profiling counter.[trace] ( advice -- ) private       Primitive advice function for black-box tracing of function       calls. The entry and exit of the function call are printed       together with the name of the function and the status of the       stack.[break] ( advice -- ) private       Primitive advice function which allows a simple break point       command loop. The commands are currently: a(bort), c(ontinue),       e(xecute), p(rofile) and r(eturn). The e(xecute) command calls       the function and returns to the break point command loop.       The e(xecute) performs the function in the normal manner       without returning to the command loop. The p(rofile) command       print the profile counter for the broken function. And last       the r(eturn) command exits the command loop without performing       the function.tail-recurse ( -- ) compilation immediate       Redefinition of the tail recursion compilation word to make it       work correctly in this context.?advice ( entry -- flag)       Verifies that the entry passed as a parameter is an advice        function.advice ( action -- )       Used in the form:               ' <advice-action> advice <advice-colon-definition>       Make the parameter action the advice action for an advice       colon definition. The colon definition is verified before       the assignment is performed. The advice action should be       a function which receives an advice block and performs some       action on it. Resets the profile information.colon ( -- )       Used in the form:               colon <advice-colon-definition>       To make an advice colon definition a "normal" function again.       An error message is given if the succeeding symbol is not of        correct type.trace ( -- )       Used in the form:               trace <advice-colon-definition>       To make an advice colon definition a traced function. An       error message is given if the succeeding symbol is not of        correct type.break ( -- )       Used in the form:               break <advice-colon-definition>       To make an advice colon definition function with a break point.       An error message is given if the succeeding symbol is not of        correct type..r ( n w -- )       Prints the number, "n", right aligned in a field with width, "w"..profile ( -- )       Scans through the vocabulary and prints the profile information       for advice functions. Prints the number of calls and the name       of the functions.: ( -- )       Redefinition of "colon" to allow easy debugging of "any" code       definitions without rewriting.SEE ALSO       compiler(1), blocks(2), structures(2), forth(1)COPYING       Copyright (C) 1989 Mikael R.K. Patel       Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies       of this manual provided the copyright notice and this permission       notice are preserved on all copies.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute modified versions       of this manual under the conditions for verbatim copying,        provided also that the section entitled "GNU General Public       License" is included exactly as in the original, and provided       that the entire resulting derived work is distributed under       the terms of a permission notice identical to this one.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute translations 